From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:46:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: NVK_DISPATCH_PROFILE, GPU time per dispatch and compute
 shader

NVK_PASS_PROFILE times runs of dispatches outside render passes but cannot
say which compute shaders take the time.  NVK_DISPATCH_PROFILE=1 (alone or
with NVK_PASS_PROFILE) puts a compute-class report behind a WAIT_FOR_IDLE
right before and right after every launch -- vkCmdDispatch,
vkCmdDispatchBase, vkCmdDispatchIndirect, the driver's own dispatches, and
each vkCmdExecuteGeneratedCommandsEXT of compute commands as a whole -- in
the pass profile's ring, harvest thread and file (NVK_PASS_PROFILE_FILE,
else %ProgramData%\Helios\nvk-pass-<pid>.txt on Windows).

Each sample is keyed by the shader's source hash, its code hash and its
workgroup size.  The source hash (vk_shader::src_hash, set by the common
compute pipeline and shader object code) is the 16-digit hash in the
SPIR-V's OpString "<hash>.dxil", which vkd3d-proton writes into every DXIL
shader and uses to name its VKD3D_SHADER_DUMP_PATH files, else FNV-1a 64
of the SPIR-V.  The code hash is the one NVK_SHADER_STATS prints.  Direct
dispatches record their grid; indirect ones have their arguments copied by
the compute engine (the I2M copy that patches the QMD) into a mapped buffer
before they launch.

Every two seconds a table, heaviest first: GPU ms/s, share of all dispatch
time, calls/s, mean, median and maximum us per call, the shader's GPRs,
warps per SM, instructions, static cycles, spills, SLM and shared memory,
the most common grids and the workgroup count range, and the indirect,
device-generated and meta-operation calls.

The waits serialize the dispatches, so the frame is slower than without
the profile; the numbers are for attributing time to shaders.  The reports
use the compute class only, so command buffers of the async compute family
stay on their compute-only channel; their dispatches are timed there, next
to the graphics queue's work (NVK_RM_ASYNC_COMPUTE=0 times them on the
graphics channel alone).
